452	// Failure-path black-box tests.
453	//
454	// Each of these drives `execute_extension` through the real compiled wasm
455	// module against a deliberately broken environment and asserts the
456	// *response* is a clean, structured failure (non-zero `exit_code`, a
457	// populated `report.error`) -- not merely that the Extism wire call itself
458	// didn't trap. `call_func_with` returning `Ok(ExecuteExtensionOutput { .. })`
459	// at all, for every scenario below, is itself already evidence supporting
460	// this crate's "execute_extension never panics; it catches everything into
461	// the report" claim: a real Rust panic inside the wasm guest surfaces to
462	// `call_func_with` as an `Err` (a wasmtime trap), not a successfully
463	// decoded `ExecuteExtensionOutput`. If any of these scenarios actually
464	// panicked, the `.expect(...)` on the wire call itself would fail, not the
465	// content assertions after it.
466	// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
467	
468	/// Part A #1 (and the strengthened replacement for the old
469	/// "runs_without_erroring_on_basic_args" test's `args: ["status"]` case):
470	/// `execute_extension` against a workspace with a working `moon` (so
471	/// project discovery succeeds) but no `.git` directory at all.
472	///
473	/// IMPORTANT finding from writing this test: a missing `.git` directory is
474	/// NOT actually a failure condition here, contrary to this task's initial
475	/// assumption. `callisto_graph::tags::fetch_all_tags` (the CommandRunner
476	/// fallback `TagIndex::build` always takes on `wasm32`, per the doc comment
477	/// on `execute_extension_status_succeeds_against_real_repo_fixture` above)
478	/// calls `runner.run("git", ["tag", "--list"], root)?` -- but `?` only
479	/// short-circuits on the *process itself* failing to spawn, not on a
480	/// non-zero exit code. When `root` has no `.git` anywhere in its ancestry,
481	/// real `git tag --list` there exits non-zero ("not a git repository") with
482	/// empty stdout, which `runner.run` reports as a perfectly normal
483	/// `Ok(CommandOutput { exit_code: Some(128), stdout: "", .. })` -- so
484	/// `fetch_all_tags` returns `Ok(vec![])` (no tags), and `status` proceeds
485	/// to report the package with no `lastTag` and `changedSinceLastTag: true`
486	/// (unreleased), not an error. This is arguably the *correct*, more robust
487	/// behavior for a brand new/pre-git package -- so this test asserts that
488	/// real, graceful-success behavior rather than forcing a fabricated
489	/// "failure" assertion that doesn't match reality.
490	#[tokio::test(flavor = "multi_thread")]
491	async fn execute_extension_no_git_repo_succeeds_with_no_last_tag_not_panic() {
